    "body": "## Summary\n- add Nginx per-peer handshake rate limits and concurrent connection caps for native WebSocket ingress\n- give SockJS a separate, higher transport budget while still bounding pre-auth traffic\n- cap ingress request bodies, disable proxy buffering, and bound upstream timeouts\n- add a runtime smoke that opens real WebSocket upgrades, verifies the ninth concurrent connection is rejected with 429, and verifies rapid handshake bursts hit the rate limiter\n- document the trusted-client-address boundary and multi-instance deployment requirements\n\n## Safety\n- complements the existing authenticated STOMP per-account limiter instead of replacing authorization\n- limits are keyed from Nginx `$remote_addr`, not spoofable forwarding headers\n- no schema change; Flyway migration not required\n\n## Validation\n- full API Maven verify, frontend test/audit/lint/build, production Compose contract and runtime container smoke are required before merge\n",
